  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set that maps this regression end-to-end:\n\n**Babel side:**\n- `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2014 the branch point: `legacy: true` (or `version: \"legacy\"`) routes to the pre-TC39 visitor; any other `version` routes to `createClassFeaturePlugin` (stage-3 TC39 semantics). This is where \"stage-2 legacy form vs stage-3 form\" is decided.\n- `packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/transformer-legacy.ts` \u2014 the actual legacy transform (`applyDecoratedDescriptor`/`__decorate`-style calls). Critically, it never emits `design:type`/`design:paramtypes` metadata or touches `Reflect.metadata`.\n- `packages/babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` \u2014 confirms Babel's TS transform only strips types/handles class-field stripping; it has no decorator-metadata emission logic at all.\n- `packages/babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts`, `babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/{index,decorators,typescript}.ts` \u2014 the plugin-ordering contract (`typescript.ts` literally throws telling users transform-typescript must run before class-feature/decorator plugins) that governs how `preset-typescript` + `proposal-decorators` compose.\n\n**SWC side:**\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs` \u2014 dispatches on `Config.legacy`/`Config.emit_metadata` to either the legacy visitor or the TC39 `Decorators` folder; TC39 path explicitly `unimplemented!()`s if metadata is requested.\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/legacy/mod.rs` and `.../legacy/metadata.rs` \u2014 the key divergence: SWC's legacy decorator pass, ported straight from the third-party `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`, natively emits `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` via `ts_metadata`/`Reflect.metadata` calls whenever `emit_metadata` (i.e. `decoratorMetadata`) is true \u2014 something Babel never does out of the box.\n- `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` \u2014 wires `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` \u2192 `Config.legacy` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` \u2192 `Config.emit_metadata`, both defaulting to `false`.\n- `crates/swc/src/builder.rs` \u2014 the pass-ordering pipeline showing where the decorators/class-feature passes sit relative to the rest of the transform chain.\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/src/typescript.rs` \u2014 confirms (absence of any \"decorator\" handling) that SWC's TS strip pass is fully decoupled from decorator/metadata emission, which lives entirely in the proposal-decorators crate.\n- `bindings/binding_core_wasm/src/types.rs` \u2014 the public `.swcrc` schema doc-comments for `legacyDecorator`/`decoratorMetadata`, i.e. what the customer actually sets in config.\n\nThe regression root cause these files establish: NestJS DI needs `design:paramtypes` metadata written to each class, which Babel's decorator pipeline never produces natively (a separate community plugin is required), while SWC produces it only when **both** `legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true` are set \u2014 the customer's SWC config almost certainly has the former (needed just to parse/emit the decorator call shape NestJS expects) but not the latter, so `Reflect.metadata`/`design:paramtypes` never gets attached and `Reflect.getMetadata` returns `undefined` at DI-resolution time.",
